        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, April 21, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, June 1, 2025</p><p>ORD C36659 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.08.030">Section 12.08.030</a> Weight Limit Imposed<br />
        <p>Excluding authorized buses, emergency vehicles, public utility vehicles, and solid waste disposal vehicles, no person may operate a vehicle exceeding ten thousand pounds gross weight on any street that is:</p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>not designated an arterial street or neighborhood collector arterial, or<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>specifically prohibited by resolution of the city council;</li></ol>
        <p>except for such local operations on other streets as is necessary to reach the vehicle’s destination or for pickup or delivery. </p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.08.040">Section 12.08.040</a> Official Arterial Street Map<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The arterials within the City of Spokane are hereby designated and classified on the&nbsp;<a href="https://static.spokanecity.org/documents/smc/maps/official-arterial-street-map-changes-map-2025.pdf" style="color:#467886; text-decoration:underline">Official Arterial Street Map</a>&nbsp;that is maintained by the city engineer. Changes to the&nbsp;<a href="https://static.spokanecity.org/documents/smc/maps/official-arterial-street-map-changes-map-2025.pdf" style="color:#467886; text-decoration:underline">Official Arterial Street Map</a>&nbsp;require city council approval.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">This section does not preclude arterial streets from being further designated for transportation planning purposes in the Comprehensive Plan.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 2, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, March 12, 2026</p><p>ORD C36823 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.08.050">Section 12.08.050</a> Motorist Information Signs<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">&ldquo;Motorist information sign&rdquo; is a sign erected or installed as a supplemental direction sign to direct motorists to motorist service businesses qualified for specific information panels pursuant to chapter 47.42 RCW in any location on, or adjacent to, the right-of-way of any roads or streets within the City of Spokane or on private property.<br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">Motorist information signs and their locations shall comply with all applicable provisions of this chapter, sections 131 and 315 of Title 23, United States Code, and such regulations as may be adopted by the Washington State department of transportation, including the Manual on Uniform Traffic Control Devices for Streets and Highways.<br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">The City is authorized to permit the erection of motorist information signs adjacent to City streets or roads or on private property. The City shall charge reasonable fees for the display of individual business signs to defray the costs of their installation and maintenance. The City shall erect and maintain the information panels. Compensation to the City shall be derived solely from the reasonable fees which it will be permitted to charge participating businesses for making and exhibiting business signs and displays.</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 25, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, August 4, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C34053 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=12.08.060">Section 12.08.060</a> Festival Streets Designated<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">It is a priority of the City of Spokane that special events primarily occur within Spokane Parks, however, the City may designate certain portions of City streets as &ldquo;festival streets&rdquo; to facilitate recurring temporary closure of vehicular traffic for large pedestrian-oriented festivals and special events that take place outside of Spokane Parks.</span></span><br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The following streets shall be considered festival streets to facilitate the recurring temporary closure of vehicle traffic for large pedestrian-oriented festivals and special events:</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
